.TH UIB 7 "2026-08-22" "UIB 0.1" "UIB Manual"
.SH NAME
uib \- user\-space RDMA protocols and libibverbs provider
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
# Direct UIB API
cc application.c \-luib

# Transparent libibverbs interposition
LD_PRELOAD=/path/to/libuibv.so application [arguments]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
UIB implements RDMA data paths in user space. Applications may link
directly with libuib and use the uib_* or uibv_* interfaces, or load
libuibv.so into an unmodified dynamically linked libibverbs program
with LD_PRELOAD.
.PP
A context selects a wire protocol independently from its transport.
The available protocols are RoCEv2, Ultra Ethernet, and a dummy test
protocol. The transports include synchronous UDP, asynchronous UDP
using an io_uring worker, AF_XDP, and TCP devmem where their platform
requirements are available.
.PP
UIB provides protection domains, registered host and DMA-BUF memory,
queue pairs, completion queues, completion-event channels, SEND,
RDMA READ and WRITE, atomics, retransmission, packet reordering, UET
NSCC congestion control, multipath, and optional zero-copy paths.
.PP
The transparent provider adds the synthetic uib0 device as the first
device returned by ibv_get_device_list(). Programs which default to
the first device therefore do not need an explicit device argument.
.SH TRANSPARENT LIBIBVERBS EXAMPLE
The following runs the unmodified perftest ib_write_bw program
between two hosts. Start the server whose UIB data-plane address is
192.0.2.1:
.nf
env LD_PRELOAD=/absolute/path/to/libuibv.so \e
    UIB_PROTOCOL=rocev2 \e
    UIB_TRANSPORT_MODE=udp\-io\-uring \e
    UIB_UDP_MODE=socket \e
    UIB_BIND_IP=192.0.2.1 UIB_BIND_PORT=4791 \e
    ib_write_bw \-i 1 \-x 0 \-\-connection=RC \e
        \-\-size=65536 \-\-iters=10000 \-\-report_gbits \-F
.fi
.PP
Run the client on 192.0.2.2, passing the server address to perftest:
.nf
env LD_PRELOAD=/absolute/path/to/libuibv.so \e
    UIB_PROTOCOL=rocev2 \e
    UIB_TRANSPORT_MODE=udp\-io\-uring \e
    UIB_UDP_MODE=socket \e
    UIB_BIND_IP=192.0.2.2 UIB_BIND_PORT=4791 \e
    ib_write_bw \-i 1 \-x 0 \-\-connection=RC \e
        \-\-size=65536 \-\-iters=10000 \-\-report_gbits \e
        \-F 192.0.2.1
.fi
.PP
The perftest TCP connection exchanges endpoint metadata; benchmark
WRITE traffic uses UIB. The -d uib0 option is optional. Both hosts
must use the same protocol and data port. Socket mode requires no
raw network capability; raw RoCEv2 RXE interoperability needs
CAP_NET_RAW.
